{"id":"word:hebrew:H2428","type":"word","title":"חַיִל","subtitle":"H2428 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"probably a force , whether of men, means or other resources; an army , wealth , virtue , valor , strength","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חַיִל (H2428) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 234 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חַיִל (chayil) means probably a force , whether of men, means or other resources; an army , wealth , virtue , valor , strength First listed occurrence: 1Chr 5 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חַיִל","transliteration":"chayil","pronunciation":"khah'-yil","strong":"H2428","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2428","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["חָ֑יִל","חָֽיִל","חַ֖יִל","חַ֔יִל","חֵ֣יל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",100],["HNcmsc",25],["HTd/Ncmsa",21],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",15],["HTd/Ncmpa",14],["HR/Ncmsa",12],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",7],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",6],["HNcmpa",5],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"probably a force , whether of men, means or other resources; an army , wealth , virtue , valor , strength","usage":"able, activity, ( ) army, band of men (soldiers), company, (great) forces, goods, host, might, power, riches, strength, strong, substance, train, ( ) valiant(-ly), valour, virtuous(-ly), war, worthy(-ily).","full":"H2428. chayil חַ֫יִל 244 noun masculine 2Kin 10:2 strength, efficiency, wealth, army ; — absolute ׳ח Gen 47:6 +, חָ֑יִל Psalm 60:14 +, חָ֑יִל Psalm 60:14 +, חֵיל Isa 36:2 ; 2Kin 18:17 ; construct חֵיל Exod 14:28 + (on Psa 10:10 see חלכה ); suffix חֵילִי Job 31:25 2 t.; חֵילְךָ Jer 15:13 +; חֵילוֺ Exod 14:4 +, etc.; plural חֲיָלִים 1Chr 7:5 19 t.; suffix חֵילֵיהֶם Isa 30:6 ; &#8212; 1 strength , usually physical: a. seldom alone (chiefly in poetry) 1Sam 2:4 ; Psa 18:33 , 40 = 2Sam 22:33 , 40 ; also ח ׳נָָּֽברוּ Job 21:7 , compare Eccl 10:10 ; אֶלחָֿ֑יִל מֵחַיִל Psa 84:8 ; ח ׳בְּכֹחַ 2Chr 26:13 ; of virility Prov 31:3 ; of ׳י s power Psa 59:12 ; 110:3 , compare Hab 3:19 ; strength of horse Psa 33:17 ; figurative of product of vine and fig-tree Joel 2:22 (|| מְּרִי ). b. of result or display of strength ח ׳עשׂה achieve might = do valiantly Num 24:18 (JE), 1Sam 14:48 ; Psalm 60:14 = Psalm 108:14; Psa 118:15-16 ,. c. often in phrases ׳גִּבּוֺרֵי(הַ)ח ׳גִּבּוֺר(הַ)ח, hero(es) of strength, mighty man (men) of valour Josh 1:14 (D), 6:2 ; 8:3 ; 10:7 (all J E), Judg 6:12 ; 11:1 ; 1Sam 9:1 ; 16:18 ; 1Kin 11:28 ; 2Kin 5:1 ; 15:20 ; 24:14 , 16 ; 1Chr 5:24 ; 7:2 , 9 ; 8:40 +? ח גבורי וכל ׳הַגִּבּוֺרִים 28:1 ; also ׳ג ׳ח 2Chr 13:3 (|| ׳ג מלחמה ); ׳ג (הַ)חֲיָלִים 1Chr 7:5 , 7 , 11 , 40 ; 11:26 (see also גִּבּוֺר , p. 150); ׳בְּנֵי(הַ)ח ׳בֶּןֿ(הַ)ח, Deut 3:18 ; Judg 18:2 + (see בֵּן 8 , p. 121); ח ׳אַנְשֵׁי ח, ׳אִישׁ Judg 3:29 ; 20:44 ; 20:46 ; 1Sam 31:12 ; 1 Samuel 11:16; 2Sam 23:20 (Qr; Kt חי , on phrase חיל בןאֿישׁ compare Dr) = 1Chr 11:22 (Kt חיל ), 2Sam 24:9 ; Nahum 2:4 ; Jer 48:15 ; 1Chr 10:12 ; Neh 11:6 ; Psa 76:6 ; ironical ׳א ׳ח שֵׁכָר לִמְסֹךְ Isa 5:22 = (|| יין לשׁתות גבורים ); Eccl 12:3 metaphor of legs. 2 ability, efficiency , often involving moral worth ח ׳אַנְשֵׁי Gen 47:6 (J), Exod 18:21 , 25 (both E); of a woman ׳ח אֵשֶׁת Prov 12:4 ; 31:10 ; Ruth 3:11 ; compare 1Kin 1:42 , 52 (opposed to רעה ), and especially ח ׳אַנְשֵׁי בָּ֑צַע שׂנְאֵי אֱמֶת אַנְשֵׁי אלהים יִרְאֵי Exod 18:21 (E); חיל עָשָׂה Prov 31:29 do worthily, efficiently , perhaps also Ruth 4:11 ; late (with weakened meaning of גִּבּוֺר ) הָאלהים בֵּית עֲבוֺדַת מְלֶאכֶת חֵיל גִּבּוֺרֵי 1Chr 9:13 , compare ח ׳אישׁ לַעֲבֹדָה בַּכִּחַ 26:8 . So also 1Sam 10:26 (read ח ׳בְּנֵי , see ᵐ5 We Dr, men of worth , opposed to בליעל בני 10:27 ) for ׳ח ᵑ0 force, band . 3 wealth Gen 34:29 = Num 31:9 (both P), Deut 8:17-18 , 33:11 ; Isa 8:4 ; 10:14 ; 30:6 (|| אוֺצְרֹתָם ), 60:5 (|| יָם הֲמוֺן ) 60:11 ; 61:6 ; Micah 4:13 ; Jer 15:13 ; 17:3 (both || אצרות ), Zeph 1:13 ; Ezek 26:12 ; 28:4-5 , (twice in verse); Zech 14:14 ; Job 5:5 ; 15:29 ; 20:15 , 18 ; 31:25 ; Psa 49:7 ; 49:11 ; 62:11 ; 73:12 ; Prov 13:22 . 4 force, army , very often Exod 14:4 , 9 , 17 , 28 (all P), 15:4 (song), 1Sam 17:20 ; 2Sam 8:9 ; 2Kin 6:4 , 15 ; 25:1 , 5 (twice in verse); 25:10 ; 2Chr 13:3 ( מלחמה גִּבּוֺרֵי בְּחַיִל ), 14:7 ; 16:7 ; 23:14 +; so usually Jeremiah: Jer 32:2 ; 34:1 +; frequently Ezekiel: Ezek 17:17 ; 27:10 +; Dan 11:7 , 13 , 25 (twice in verse); 11:26 ; = a band 1Sam 10:26 ( ᵑ0 , but see 2 , adfin. ); of train of Queen of Sheba ׳ח גדול 1Kin 10:2 2Chr 9:1 ; כָּבֵד חֵיל Isa 36:1 = 2Kin 18:17 a powerful army (on form compare Sta § 194 c ); also (late) הַצָּבָא חֵיל 1Chr 20:1 ; 2Chr 26:13 , עָם חֵיל Est 8:11 ; חֲיָלִים הֲמוֺן Dan 11:10 ; ׳שַׂרהֿח 2Sam 24:2 = captain of the host , הח ׳שָׂרֵי 24:4 ; 24:4 ; הַחֲיָלִים שָׂרֵי captains of armies (bands, divisions) 1Kin 15:20 2Chr 16:4 ; 2Kin 25:23 ; Jer 40:7 , 13 ; 41:11 , 13 , 16 ; 42:1 , 8 ; 43:4-5 ,. החִיל מִּקּוּדֵי Num 31:14 (P). — חֵילוּ Ezek 32:31 omitted by B Hi Co: for חֵילֵךְ 27:11 read probably a proper name, of a location, compare Da; Co proposes חתלון (compare 47:15 ; 48:1 ), Hal MÈl. Epigr. 1874, 69 חלך = Cilicia , see Lag M i. 211 . חַ֫יִל noun masculine power, strength, army (see Biblical Hebrew II. חיל חול, ); — 1 power: absolute וְחָ֑יִל בְּאֶדְרָע Ezra 4:23 by force and power ; בְח ׳קרא i.e. call loudly Dan 3:4 , בְּחַיִל 4:11 ; 5:7 ; ׳גִּבָּרֵיאח 3:20 mighty men of power. 2 force, army , suffix חֵילֵהּ Dan 3:20 ; construct שְׁמַיָּא חֵיל 4:32 (= Biblical Hebrew הַשָּׁמַיִם צְכָא ).","rootNote":"from 2342 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 5 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 5 18","1Chr 5 24","1Chr 7 2","1Chr 7 5","1Chr 7 7","1Chr 7 9","1Chr 7 11","1Chr 7 40"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":234,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 5 18","book":"1Chr","chapter":5,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חַיִל֒","source":"hebr